  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "publlic access currently requires authn as per ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2632"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2632",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Fedora should be configurable to allow anonymous access (i.e. on a read-only basis) to resources, whenever allowed by WebAC.   One possible approach is to assign a single webac agent URI (e.g something like ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora.info/local-user#Anonymous)"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora.info/local-user#Anonymous)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " in the absence of any user principal provided by authn.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
