       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Aaron Birkland",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Right now, Fedora will accept un-authenticated requests and do the Right Thing (allow access if it has been granted to \"evertbody\" as per webac).  However, authentication is presumed to be external (container auth, or shib proxy, etc)</p>\n\n\n<p>This ticket has been re-scoped to documentation.  In particular, document that:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>authn is external to the repository right now</li>\n\t<li>The repository will accept un-authenticated requests and apply webac policies as expected</li>\n\t<li>Therefore, Fedora is OK with you expose some fcrepo resources in an un-authenticated manner, but cannot currently help you do that (as it is external)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>That being said, the Shiro architecture brings the possibility of bringing authn realms into shiro.  Long-term, this opens the door to allowing Fedora to control the presence or absence of authn for individual resources</p>",
     "created": "16/Aug/18 1:03 PM",
     "id": "20138",
     "jsdPublic": true,
