  "description": "<p>publlic access currently requires authn as per <a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2632\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2632</a></p>\n\n<p>Fedora should be configurable to allow anonymous access (i.e. on a read-only basis) to resources, whenever allowed by WebAC.   One possible approach is to assign a single webac agent URI (e.g something like <a href=\"http://fedora.info/local-user#Anonymous\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora.info/local-user#Anonymous</a>) in the absence of any user principal provided by authn.  </p>",
